{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":4072055,"ns":0,"title":"Cogging torque","extract":"In electromechanics, the cogging torque of electrical motors is the torque due to the interaction between the permanent magnets of the rotor and the stator slots of a permanent magnet machine. It is also known as detent or no-current torque.","description":"Torque in electrical motors","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}